// REQUIRES: long
// P04.01: the second half of linear.long.test: GIR of chains of named types.
// Chains of named types (review R6): the glue and the lowering of a type walk
// it on stacks of their own, and a part of the type deeper than 24 levels is
// compared by a function of its own (Glue.cpp), so the time stays near-linear.
// The text of an array chain prints the whole type at every use, so only its
// bitstream is timed.
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-gir-linear.py --gopp %gopp --gen %S/Inputs/gen-gir-stress.py --out %t.d typestruct 5000
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-gir-linear.py --gopp %gopp --gen %S/Inputs/gen-gir-stress.py --out %t.d --emits girb typearr 5000
// A chain of 20000 (arrays) or 10000 (structs: LLVM's own StructType::setBody
// is quadratic in the chain) is lowered, with == and a copy, to an object file,
// within a CPU-time ceiling of three times the cost alone, counted in units
// of `gopp version` (tests/cpu-limit.py),
// never a wall-clock limit; the growth is judged by the two checks above.
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-gir-stress.py typearr 20000 > %t.arr.gopp
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-gir-stress.py typestruct 10000 > %t.st.gopp
// RUN: %{cpu_limit} 24 62 -- %gopp build -emit=girb %t.arr.gopp -o %t.arr.girb
// RUN: %{cpu_limit} 475 405 -- %gopp build -emit=obj %t.arr.gopp -o %t.arr.o
// RUN: %{cpu_limit} 132 167 -- %gopp build -emit=obj %t.st.gopp -o %t.st.o
